1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
One checkout click. The screen times out. But the payment request might still be running.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Java futures can complete exceptionally while an external payment call continues. Timeout does not mean rollback.

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Run independent stock and shipping reads concurrently, using a bounded executor and real deadlines.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Before charging, persist a checkout attempt and send a stable provider idempotency key.

5
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:00,000
If the response is uncertain, return pending, reconcile through signed webhooks and provider status, and never blindly charge again.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Publish fulfillment only after confirmed payment, through a transactional outbox. Reliable checkout tells the truth when networks fail.
